=== Q4VCM1 GO:0080096 (VERDICT missing) ===
THINKING: The GO term is "phosphatidate-sterol O-acyltransferase activity" with the definition that it catalyzes the reaction between a phosphatidate and a sterol to form a sterol ester and lysophosphatidate. This primary reaction involves the transfer of an acyl group from phosphatidate to sterol, which is a specific enzymatic mechanism. The protein Q4VCM1 has three ACT_SITE annotations: one at 194-195 with evidence ECO:0000255 and notes about an acyl-ester intermediate, another at 460-461 with evidence ECO:0000250 and notes about a charge relay system, and a third at 504-505 with the same evidence and note. The only annotation that directly relates to the primary reaction of acyl transfer is the ACT_SITE at 194-195. The other annotations are about charge relay systems, which are secondary consequences or unrelated to the core function of the GO term. Therefore, the ACT_SITE at 194-195 most plausibly explains why Q4VCM1 carries the term "phosphatidate-sterol O-acyltransferase activity."

FEATURE: ACT_SITE 194-195
